## A carousel

{% carousel caption="Three placeholder slides, each cropped to its own aspect ratio." %}
{% slide %}
![First slide](../../assets/writing/example-slide-1.svg)
{% /slide %}
{% slide ratio="1/1" %}
![Second slide](../../assets/writing/example-slide-2.svg)
{% /slide %}
{% slide ratio="3/4" %}
![Third slide](../../assets/writing/example-slide-3.svg)
{% /slide %}
{% /carousel %}

The track runs across the whole screen while the first slide lines up with the text. The arrows sit below it, aligned with the start of the text, and move one slide at a time. Each slide can be cropped to its own aspect ratio; the first one keeps its original shape.

## Code, quotes and tables

```ts
export function greet(name: string) {
  return `Hello, ${name}. This line is long enough to need horizontal scrolling inside the code block on a narrow screen.`;
}
```

> A blockquote keeps its text on the column while the tinted box flows past it.

| Element     | Flows out | Text stays on the column |
| ----------- | --------- | ------------------------ |
| Code block  | Yes       | No                       |
| Image       | Yes       | Caption only             |
| Table       | Yes       | No                       |
| Blockquote  | Yes       | Yes                      |

## Math

Inline math sits in a sentence, like {% inlineMath expression="e^{i\\pi} + 1 = 0" /%}, and block math gets its own line.

{% math expression="\\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx = \\frac{1}{3}" /%}

